<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 7 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Money and Trade</h1><p class="path-tagline">The routes, coins and companies that moved the world.</p><p class="path-intro">Armies take headlines, but trade pays for them. This path follows wealth through history, silk and spice, caravans and sea lanes, the banks that financed empires and the company that became one, asking how commerce built and broke the powers of every age.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Builder</a> · <a href="/start">the Navigator</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/silk"><span class="path-step-ph">1</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Term</span><span class="path-step-name">Silk</span><span class="path-step-why">The fibre that named a road and moved ideas along with cloth.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/trans-saharan-trade"><span class="path-step-ph">2</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Term</span><span class="path-step-name">Trans-Saharan trade</span><span class="path-step-why">Gold north, salt south: the caravans that made Ghana, Mali and Songhai.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean-trade"><span class="path-step-ph">3</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Encyclopedia · Term</span><span class="path-step-name">Indian Ocean trade</span><span class="path-step-why">The monsoon exchange that linked Africa, Arabia, India and China long before Europeans arrived.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/spice-trade"><span class="path-step-ph">4</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Encyclopedia · Term</span><span class="path-step-name">Spice trade</span><span class="path-step-why">Cloves and pepper: small cargoes worth fortunes, and the wars fought to corner them.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/republic-of-venice"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paolo-lucio-anafesto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Profile · 697 CE – 1797 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Republic of Venice</span><span class="path-step-why">The middleman city that grew rich on the eastern trade and fought to keep it.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">6 · Encyclopedia · Institution</span><span class="path-step-name">Dutch East India Company</span><span class="path-step-why">The joint-stock company with a flag, an army and an empire of its own.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/bank-of-amsterdam"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bank-of-amsterdam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">7 · Encyclopedia · Institution · 1609–1820</span><span class="path-step-name">Bank of Amsterdam</span><span class="path-step-why">The bank at the heart of the first modern financial centre.</span></span></a></li></ol>
